{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"According to the Mean Value Theorem, there exists a number $c$ in the open interval $4\u003cx\u003c12$ such that $f'(c)$ is equal to the average rate of change of $f$ over the interval:\n\n$f'(c)=\\dfrac{f(12)-f(4)}{(12)-(4)}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"First, let's find that average rate of change:\n\n$\\dfrac{f(12)-f(4)}{(12)-(4)}=\\dfrac{5-3}{8}=\\blueD{\\dfrac{1}{4}}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Now, let's differentiate $f$ and find the $x$-value for which $f'(x)=\\blueD{\\dfrac{1}{4}}$.\n\n$f'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}$ [[☃ explanation 1]]\n\nThe solution of $f'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{4}$ is $x=7.5$.  [[☃ explanation 2]]\n\n$x=7.5$ is indeed within the interval $4\u003cx\u003c12$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nf'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\sqrt{2x+1}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(2x+1)^{\\large\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2}(2x+1)^{\\large -\\frac{1}{2}}\\dfrac{d}{dx}(2x+1)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+1}}(2)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}},"explanation 2":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nf'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{4}\n\\\\\\\\\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{4}\n\\\\\\\\\n\\sqrt{2x+1}\u0026=4\n\\\\\\\\\n(\\sqrt{2x+1})^2\u0026=4^2\n\\\\\\\\\n2x+1\u0026=16\n\\\\\\\\\n2x\u0026=15\n\\\\\\\\\nx\u0026=7.5\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $c=7.5$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $f(x)=\\sqrt{2x+1}$ and let $c$ be the number that satisfies the Mean Value Theorem for $f$ on the interval $4\\leq x\\leq12$.\n\n**What is $c$ ?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$0$","correct":false},{"content":"$1.5$","correct":false},{"content":"$4$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$7.5$","correct":true,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
